Day 1 — Docker & Containerization

Today I started learning Docker and containerization.

Topics studied
What containerization is and why it is used.
Why Docker is useful for:
Reproducibility
Dependency management
Portability
Version consistency
Evolution from:
Physical servers
Virtualization
Virtual Machines
Containers
Difference between Virtual Machines and Containers.
Understood that VMs run a complete guest OS, while containers share the host OS kernel.
Understood that both VMs and containers still use the host's physical resources such as CPU and RAM.
Main advantage of containers: they avoid the overhead of running a separate OS/kernel for every application.
Understood the basic idea of Docker architecture.
Learned about Docker's role in creating and running containers.
Started learning how Docker can be used in AWS/cloud environments.
Set up/learned about Docker on an Ubuntu environment
